ation expose `toBytes()` and `fromBytes()`. CUID v2 and Nanoid expose a smaller API because they have no canonical byte representation. UUID v5 is the one generator that takes an input: it derives the same ID from the same name and namespace, and adds `namespace()` plus the RFC 9562 namespace constants."},"137":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"Each generator reference lists the exact call signatures, methods, constants, and overloads available from its imported value."},"138":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Each format is independently importable and tree-shakeable. Install one package, then ship only the strategy your application imports."},"139":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Strategy"},"140":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Direct import"},"141":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Usual function call"},"142":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Primary value"},"143":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"UUID v4"},"144":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`uniku/uuid/v4`"},"145":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs