303":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"Nanoid (10 chars)"},"304":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`nanoid@6.0.2`"},"305":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~0.6–0.65×"},"306":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"Same, with a shorter output"},"307":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"CUID2"},"308":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`@paralleldrive/cuid2@3.3.0`"},"309":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~7–9×"},"310":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"SHA3-512 over time, salt, counter, and fingerprint"},"311":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"KSUID"},"312":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`@owpz/ksuid@25.7.21`"},"313":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~1.5–1.7×"},"314":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"uniku returns a string; the reference builds a KSUID object"},"315":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"ObjectID"},"316":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`bson@7.3.4`"},"317":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~0.6–0.7×"},"318":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"Both cache the process-random field and increment a 24-bit counter"},"319":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"TSID"},"320":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`tsid-ts@0.0.9`"},"321":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~2–2.6×"},"322":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"uniku returns a `bigint`; the reference builds a TSID object"},"323":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"XID"},"324":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"`nexid@2.1.0`"},"325":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"\\~1.3×"},"326":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#generation-speed","content":"Both encode seconds, identity, and a 24-bit counter"},"327":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"**They are not reproducible to the digit.** Two runs of the same command on the\nsame machine moved the small-ratio rows by up to 22% (UUID v4, TSID, ObjectID,\nXID), and a different machine moved the ULID row from 163× to \\~85×. That is why\nthe table reports ranges rounded to about one significant figure instead of the\nfour significant figures a single run prints."},"328":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"A note on provenance, so the ranges are not mistaken for something better than\nthey are: the upper bounds come from the linked CI run, which is published and\nauditable. The lower bounds and the repeat-run figures come from runs on a\nmaintainer machine (macOS arm64, Node.js `25.9.0`, same command, same commit) that\nare not published as artefacts. Re-running the commands below on your own hardware\nis the only way to get a number that applies to your hardware, and that is the\npoint — treat the table as a shape, not a scoreboard."},"329":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"**The UUID v4 row compares two wrappers, not two algorithms.** Both sides end in\nthe same native call, but not by the same route: uniku resolves\n`crypto.randomUUID` once at module load and calls the bound function, while\n`uuid@14.0.3` re-reads `crypto.randomUUID` on every invocation. Measured on a\nper-call basis that is zero property reads against two. So this row measures\nwrapper overhead on top of a shared native primitive — a real cost that callers\npay, but not evidence that uniku generates UUIDs faster, and not a noise control.\nIt is also the row that moved most between runs (1.2× to 1.6×)."},"330":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"**Two rows are not like-for-like on work done.** The TypeID, KSUID, and TSID rows\ncompare uniku returning its primary value directly against a reference that\nallocates an object first. That gap is real for callers, but it measures API shape\nas much as encoding speed."},"331":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"**The ULID row measures two different random-draw strategies.** `ulid@3.0.2` runs\n`detectPRNG()` — feature detection plus `detectRoot()` — on every `ulid()` call,\ndraws its 16 random characters through 16 separate\n`getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(1))` calls, and builds the string by prepending.\nuniku draws 16 bytes once per millisecond and increments the existing 80-bit tail\nfor every further call in that millisecond, so most iterations of a tight\nbenchmark loop perform no random draw at all. Both behaviours are deliberate, and\nboth are part of the ratio; describing only the reference's overhead would leave\nthe largest number on this page under-qualified."},"332":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#how-to-read-these-numbers","content":"**Everything here is one engine.** These are Node.js numbers on V8, and several\nhot paths are unrolled for it. Bun, Deno, and browser engines are covered by the\ncorrectness matrix, not by these measurements."},"333":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"The compatibility benchmark\nruns each implementation in a fresh process, so neither side inherits the other's\nwarmed JIT state or shared buffers. CI balances both launch orders across four\nrepetitions and reports the per-row median."},"334":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"`bench-results.ts` carries the statistics:"},"335":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"dispersion uses the median absolute deviation scaled by 1.4826 rather than a\nstandard deviation, so one noisy runner does not dominate;"},"336":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"`withinActionRme` describes spread across repetitions in one CI action and\n`crossActionRme` describes spread across historical actions;"},"337":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"a regression must exceed `max(configured threshold, 2 × combined dispersion)`\nbefore it is reported, and reference-side rows never gate a change;"},"338":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"`bench-summary` prints the combined dispersion for the ratio as a `Spread`\ncolumn, and labels a row `parity (within spread)` when its deviation from 1× is\nsmaller than that spread."},"339":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"Shared-runner benchmarks stay directional. They report possible regressions\ninstead of blocking a release, and the deterministic build, type, test,\npacked-package, runtime, and bundle checks are the actual gates."},"340":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#methodology","content":"Recorded results live in the CI run,\nand the rolling baseline\ntracks later runs."},"341":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"Every entry point is independently importable and tree-shakeable: importing\n`uniku/ulid` does not pull in the UUID, TypeID, or KSUID code. Sizes below were\nremeasured from the current source with `tsdown@0.22.3`, minification, and gzip\nlevel 9:"},"342":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"Import"},"343":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"Minified + gzipped"},"344":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/uuid/v4`"},"345":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.2 KB"},"346":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/uuid/v5`"},"347":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-85","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.8 KB"},"348":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-86","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/uuid/v7`"},"349":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-87","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.7 KB"},"350":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-88","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/ulid`"},"351":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-89","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.9 KB"},"352":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-90","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/typeid`"},"353":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-91","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~2.9 KB"},"354":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-92","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/cuid2`"},"355":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-93","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.0 KB"},"356":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-94","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/cuid/v2`"},"357":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-95","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.0 KB"},"358":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-96","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/nanoid`"},"359":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-97","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.2 KB"},"360":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-98","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/ksuid`"},"361":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-99","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.5 KB"},"362":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-100","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/objectid`"},"363":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-101","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.6 KB"},"364":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-102","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/tsid`"},"365":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-103","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.7 KB"},"366":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-104","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/xid`"},"367":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-105","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~2.1 KB"},"368":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-106","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/errors`"},"369":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-107","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~445 B"},"370":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-108","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/generators`"},"371":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-109","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~101 B"},"372":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-110","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"These numbers are reproducible byte-for-byte with `pnpm bundle:summary`."},"373":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-111","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"The CUID v2 entry point imports SHA3-512 from `@noble/hashes`, uniku's one runtime\ndependency; the size above excludes that external dependency's own weight. The\nUUID v5 entry point inlines its SHA-1, so its size includes the whole hash and it\nhas no runtime dependency."},"374":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-112","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"Run the benchmark and bundle-size tooling from the repository root:"},"375":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-113","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"`bench:compat` runs uniku and the reference packages in separate processes;\n`bench:summary` reads those results and prints a comparison table. CI repeats the\ncompatibility run four times with balanced launch orders, which is what populates\nthe `Spread` column. `bundle:summary` builds each entry point and reports its\nminified, gzipped size. `bench:cold-start` measures fresh-process startup\nseparately from warmed generation throughput."},"376":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Start here","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"377":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Eleven type-safe ID strategies behind one API, with measured performance and independent entry points."},"378":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"The library contract"},"379":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"uniku collects eleven ID generation strategies behind one consistent, type-safe API: UUID v4/v5/v7, ULID, TypeID, Nanoid, CUID v2, KSUID, ObjectID, XID, and TSID. Published benchmarks compare generation speed with dedicated npm alternatives for each format. Each strategy still has its own entry point, so your application ships only the code it imports."},"380":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install uniku\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" description=\"Generate your first ID in one import.\" icon=\"<PackageOpen />\" />"},"381":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Compare eleven strategies\" href=\"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id\" description=\"Choose a format by the job it needs to do.\" icon=\"<ScanLine />\" />"},"382":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"See the benchmarks\" href=\"/docs/guides/performance\" description=\"Compare every generator with its dedicated npm alternative.\" icon=\"<Gauge />\" />"},"383":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Browse integrations\" href=\"/docs/guides/integrations\" description=\"Start with runnable Hono, Drizzle, and Effect examples.\" icon=\"<Blocks />\" />"},"384":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Use the CLI\" href=\"/docs/cli\" description=\"Generate, inspect, and validate without writing a script.\" icon=\"<Terminal />\" />"},"385":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Migrate to uniku\" href=\"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries\" description=\"Move from a familiar ID package without changing stored identifiers.\" icon=\"<ArrowRightLeft />\" />"},"386":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Every generator import returns a callable function with precise TypeScript signatures and the helpers that make sense for its format, such as `isValid()`, `toBytes()`, `fromBytes()`, or `timestamp()`. The library is ESM-only, built on web standards, and tested end to end across Node.js, Bun, Deno, browsers, and Cloudflare Workers. The stability contract defines the entry points, validation boundaries, and runtime support policy that take effect with `uniku@1.0.0`."},"387":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Install @uniku/cli when you need an ID in a terminal, migration, or shell pipeline. It shares the library's formats but has its own release lifecycle."},"388":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"page","content":"Migrate from other libraries","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Migration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries"},"389":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-0","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Keep familiar formats while moving to direct, portable imports."},"390":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-1","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"From `uuid`"},"391":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-2","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"Name-based UUID v5"},"392":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-3","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-nanoid","content":"From `nanoid`"},"393":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-4","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-ulid","content":"From `ulid`"},"394":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-5","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-typeid-js","content":"From `typeid-js`"},"395":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-6","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-paralleldrivecuid2","content":"From `@paralleldrive/cuid2`"},"396":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-7","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-owpzksuid","content":"From `@owpz/ksuid`"},"397":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-8","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-bson","content":"From `bson`"},"398":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-9","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"From `tsid-ts`"},"399":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-10","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"From `xid-ts` or `nexid`"},"400":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-11","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Migration is usually an import change first. Keep the stored identifier format stable, then move generation behind the new direct entry point. Every example below shows the value returned by the uniku generator."},"401":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-12","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku generates UUID v4, v5, and v7. There is no uniku equivalent for v1, v3, or v6; keep the `uuid` package for those, or generate them elsewhere and only use uniku for v4, v5, and v7 values."},"402":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-13","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"The rest of `uuid`'s API maps onto uniku's per-generator methods, scoped to the version you imported:"},"403":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-14","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuid`"},"404":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-15","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku"},"405":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-16","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`parse(id)`"},"406":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-17","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.toBytes(id)` / `uuidv5.toBytes(id)` / `uuidv7.toBytes(id)` accept any UUID version, plus `NIL` and `MAX`. Unlike `parse()`, they validate only the length, the separators, and the hex characters — not the version nibble or the RFC variant"},"407":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-18","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`stringify(bytes)`"},"408":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-19","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.fromBytes(bytes)` / `uuidv5.fromBytes(bytes)` / `uuidv7.fromBytes(bytes)`"},"409":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-20","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`validate(id)`"},"410":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-21","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.isValid(id)` / `uuidv5.isValid(id)` / `uuidv7.isValid(id)`"},"411":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-22","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`version(id)`"},"412":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-23","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"Implied by which `isValid` matches: each accepts only its own version."},"413":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-24","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuid`'s `v5(name, namespace)` becomes `uuidv5(name, namespace)`, with the same argument order. The buffer form `v5(name, namespace, buf, offset)` keeps its order too. Both produce the same IDs for the same inputs, so stored v5 values stay valid."},"414":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-25","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuid`"},"415":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-26","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"uniku"},"416":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-27","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5(name, namespace)`"},"417":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-28","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5(name, namespace)`"},"418":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-29","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5(name, namespace, buf, offset)`"},"419":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-30","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5(name, namespace, buf, offset)`"},"420":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-31","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`v5.DNS` / `v5.URL`"},"421":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-32","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"`uuidv5.DNS` / `uuidv5.URL`"},"422":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-33","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#name-based-uuid-v5","content":"uniku also exposes `uuidv5.OID` and `uuidv5.X500`, and `uuidv5.namespace(ns)` to parse a namespace once for many names. See UUID v5."},"423":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-34","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-typeid-js","content":"`typeid-js` returns a TypeID object. uniku returns the canonical string directly."},"424":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-35","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"`tsid-ts` exposes a TSID object. uniku uses the native `bigint` as TSID's primary value."},"425":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-36","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"Convert at a string boundary when you need the canonical Base32 form:"},"426":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-37","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Both libraries implement the rs/xid representation. uniku returns the canonical string directly and does not require asynchronous setup."},"427":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-38","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Use `xid.toBytes(id)` and `xid.fromBytes(bytes)` when you store the 12-byte value."},"428":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-39","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"Before replacing an existing generator, test the representation you store and expose. UUIDs, ULIDs, ObjectIDs, and XIDs have canonical byte forms; Nanoid and CUID v2 are string-native."},"429":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"page","content":"Migrate to uniku v1","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Migration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1"},"430":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-0","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1","content":"Prepare for the v1 entry-point contract without changing identifier data."},"431":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-1","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"Move CUID v2 to the versioned entry point"},"432":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-2","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Update error-code matches"},"433":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-3","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#removed-codes","content":"Removed codes"},"434":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-4","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/v1#what-remains-stable","content":"What remains stable"},"435":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-5","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1","content":"uniku v1 keeps its canonical identifier formats stable while finalizing its pre-v1 entry points and machine-readable error contract."},"436":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-6","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"`uniku/cuid2` is a pre-v1 alias. Use the canonical versioned import before upgrading:"},"437":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-7","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#move-cuid-v2-to-the-versioned-entry-point","content":"The generator behavior is the same. This is an import migration, not a data migration: existing CUID v2 values remain valid."},"438":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-8","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Pre-v1 error codes included the generator name. V1 uses strategy-agnostic codes and reports the generator separately through `error.strategy`:"},"439":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-9","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`uniku/errors` exports `ERROR_CODES`, the authoritative runtime catalog, and its derived `ErrorCode` type. The `_tag` classes and human-readable messages keep their existing roles."},"440":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-10","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"This table maps every machine-readable code emitted by `uniku@0.4.3` to its v1 replacement:"},"441":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-11","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"Pre-v1 code(s)"},"442":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-12","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"V1 code"},"443":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-13","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`UUID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `ULID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `ULID_TIMESTAMP_OVERFLOW`, `KSUID_TIMESTAMP_TOO_LOW`, `KSUID_TIMESTAMP_TOO_HIGH`, `OBJECTID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `XID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `TSID_TIMESTAMP_INVALID`, `TSID_TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`"},"444":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-14","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE`"},"445":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-15","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#update-error-code-matches","content":"`UUID_INVALID_HEX_CHAR`, `ULID_INVALID_CHAR`, `KSUID_INVALID_CHAR`, `OBJECTID_INVALID_CHAR`, `XID_INVALID_CHAR`, `TSID_INVALID_CHAR`, `TYPEID_SUFFIX_INVALID_CHARACTER`"},"446":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-16","page_id":"/docs