cs/migration/v1#what-remains-stable","content":"Within `1.x`, uniku will not remove or rename documented entry points, exports, options, methods, or constants. Canonical string formats, byte order, timestamp units, and documented error codes are part of the contract."},"493":{"id":"/docs/migration/v1-63","page_id":"/docs/migration/v1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/v1#what-remains-stable","content":"Read the stability contract for the full release and runtime policy."},"494":{"id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","page_id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","type":"page","content":"CUID v2","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2"},"495":{"id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","content":"Non-sequential, string-native identifiers that resist enumeration."},"496":{"id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cuid-v2","content":"CUID v2 is for public values where predictability is the problem. It is string-native, so there is no byte codec to maintain or expose."},"497":{"id":"/docs/reference/entry-points","page_id":"/docs/reference/entry-points","type":"page","content":"Entry points","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/entry-points"},"498":{"id":"/docs/reference/entry-points-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/entry-points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/entry-points","content":"Eleven stable generator entry points behind one consistent, type-safe API."},"499":{"id":"/docs/reference/entry-points-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/entry-points","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/entry-points#how-modules-differ","content":"How modules differ"},"500":{"id":"/docs/reference/entry-points-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/entry-points","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/entry-points#generator-references","content":"Generat